course: dictionary
lesson: 1918
title: Comedian
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A comedian is a person whose job is to make people laugh, usually by telling jokes or doing funny things on stage, on TV or in films. Context gives you the clues. «An impression copies how a famous person talks and moves; comedians in many countries have mocked leaders for hundreds of years.» Comedians are the people who do the mocking, so they are funny performers who make fun of people.
explain: Comedian can also mean anyone who is always being funny, like a class comedian. Look at «a bit of a comedian» in a sentence. It describes someone who jokes around a lot, not someone with a stage job. Read the words around the word and ask what kind of person they describe.
explain: «Studio audiences are warmed up by a comedian and sometimes extra laughter is added later, so laughter does not prove a joke is funny.» The clue is the word prove. Laughter can be added on purpose, so hearing a laugh does not always mean the joke was good. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: A comedian is a person whose job is to make people laugh.
fact: A stand-up comedian performs jokes alone on stage in front of an audience.
fact: A class comedian is someone at school who is always being funny.
fact: «Comedian» is a noun, and its plural is «comedians».
fact: Laughter does not always prove a joke is funny, because some shows add extra laughter later.
exercise: What is a comedian? | A person who sings in a choir | *A person whose job is to make people laugh | A teacher who marks spelling tests
exercise: Mia says her brother is a bit of a comedian. What does she mean? | He works on a stage every night | He is a very good singer | *He is always joking and being funny | He is a doctor at the hospital
exercise: «Laughter does not prove a joke is funny.» What does this sentence tell you? | Laughter is always real and never added | *A laugh does not always mean a joke is good | Audiences never laugh at comedians | Every joke on TV is funny
test: «A stand-up comedian» works how? | In a kitchen, cooking dinner for a large group | *Alone on stage, telling jokes to an audience | Behind a desk, writing letters all day
test: «An impression copies how a famous person talks and moves.» What is an impression? | *A copy of how someone talks and moves | A long, boring speech | A loud shout that wakes everyone up | A kind of painting of a famous person
exam: Find and copy the word that means a person who makes people laugh. | *comedian | impression | studio | famous
